/* three alternating fixpoints over ground atoms; at B 0 the prover chooses
   between a cycle through B and C, whose outermost predicate B is a least
   fixpoint (lost), and a cycle through A and B, whose outermost predicate A is
   a greatest fixpoint (won): the query is true */
B 0
s.t.
A (x: int): bool =nu B 0;
B (x: int): bool =mu x = 0 /\ (C x \/ A x);
C (x: int): bool =nu B 0;
